<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austrian State Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austrian State Treaty, signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> on 15 May 1955 by the four occupying powers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, restored Austria as a sovereign, independent and democratic state. It ended the Allied occupation that had lasted since 1945, banned union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and protected the rights of minorities. It was followed in October 1955 by Austria's declaration of permanent neutrality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austrian-state-treaty.jpg" alt="Austrian State Treaty" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Master Uegly; derivative work by Hanzlan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Austria_Occupation_Zones_1945-55_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
